Licensing exception for the vendored jars in server/libs/
---------------------------------------------------------

The jars vendored in server/libs/ (gst1-java-fixups) are separate works of
their respective copyright holders, licensed under the GNU Lesser General
Public License version 3 only. They are redistributed under the terms of that
license — see server/libs/LICENSE for the notice, the license text and where
the corresponding source code lives. The MIT grant above neither applies to
nor covers those files.

The runnable server JAR produced by the build shades (embeds compiled classes
of) the LGPL-licensed gst1-java-fixups library: anyone distributing the
runnable JAR receives those embedded parts under LGPL version 3. The
corresponding source remains available in the -sources jar in server/libs/.
server/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt lists every third-party component embedded in
the JAR and its license.

Licensing exception for Apache-2.0 components in client/
--------------------------------------------------------

The following components are embedded in the client and remain licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0, as stated in their headers or package
descriptors. The full license text is in client/licenses/Apache-2.0.txt.

- WPMv2 - Webstrate Package Manager
  Copyright 2019 Rolf Bagge, Janus Bager Kristensen, CAVI - Center for
  Advanced Visualisation and Interaction, Aarhus University
  Embedded in client/prototypes/stund/index.html (and client/prototypes/stund.zip)
  and client/repository/stund.html.

- SlopScript
  Copyright 2025 Janus B. Kristensen, CAVI, Center for Advanced Visualization
  and Interaction, Aarhus University
  In client/fragment-sync/AI Integration/SlopScript.wpm/ and embedded in the
  prototype and repository files above.

- FragmentFilesystemSync (Codestrates package)
  Embedded in client/prototypes/stund/index.html (and client/prototypes/stund.zip).

Run-time dependencies
---------------------

Libraries the client loads at run time from CDNs (e.g., React and tldraw via
esm.sh) and native libraries the server expects on the system (e.g.,
GStreamer, libnice and TEN VAD) are not distributed in this repository and
remain under their own licenses. Note in particular that tldraw is not open
source: its license requires a license key for production use.
